6) Verification Plan (Verification Lead owns this section)
Owner: Dayanna Porta

Correctness checks / tests to run
- Expected results come from an independent script that checks all 4,096 subsets, so a passing test is real evidence.
- Greedy tests (highest rating first, lightest first, best rating-to-weight ratio): expected experiments, total weight, and total rating, always within the 700 kg limit.
- Brute-force tests: the optimal subset (rating 53, 692 kg) and the top three valid subsets, with ties broken in favor of the lighter set.
- Comparison summary: prints the three greedy results and the optimum, and names the same results shown in the tests above.
- Edge cases: capacity 0, 6, 7, 653, 654, and 1,309 kg, plus rating ties (experiment 10 before 2).
- General checks: weight never exceeds capacity, no experiment is repeated, and totals equal the sum of the chosen experiments.
- Regression: all earlier tests are re-run after the Week 3 Change Request.
- Evidence: results log with date, result, and a link to a commit, PR, or console output file.
- Status: test plan drafted; tests not run yet (code in progress).
